#: ../source/python/plot.rst:68
msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/python/plot.rst:70
msgid ""
"A field is not drawn directly: it is first evaluated on a *slice* of the "
"mesh (see the ``Slice`` object), then the points, simplexes and values of "
"the slice are given to the renderer as |np| arrays. This has several "
"consequences:"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/python/plot.rst:74
msgid ""
"In 3D, only the surface is drawn: the default slice operation is "
"``('boundary',)``, which keeps only the triangles of the skin of the domain."
" Any other slice operation can be passed with ``slice_op`` (planar cuts, "
"iso-values, balls, intersections, ...)."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/python/plot.rst:78
msgid ""
"High order elements and curved geometric transformations are represented by "
"refining each convex ``refine`` times (default 3 for fields)."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/python/plot.rst:80
msgid ""
"The points of the slice are not shared between convexes, so discontinuous "
"fields keep their jumps."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/python/plot.rst:82
msgid ""
"The deformation is applied by building the slice on the deformed mesh, so "
"that the colour, the arrows and the mesh edges all follow it."
msgstr ""

