#: ../source/python/plot.rst:119
msgid ""
"With Matplotlib, ``ax=`` draws in existing axes and ``(fig, ax)`` is "
"returned; use ``show=True`` to open the window. With PyVista, ``plotter=`` "
"adds to an existing ``pyvista.Plotter``, which is returned; ``axes_style`` "
"is ``'grid'`` (default, graduated axes), ``'bounds'`` or ``'triad'``, and "
"``notebook``, ``off_screen`` and ``screenshot`` are passed to PyVista."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/python/plot.rst:125
msgid ""
"``gfp.plot_slice(sl, mf, U)`` does the same for any ``Slice`` built by the "
"user, or draws the slice itself when no field is given (a slice made of "
"curves, such as streamlines, is drawn as tubes with PyVista)."
